    {"comment":"A boast ability can be activated at any point after the creature with that ability has been declared as an attacker. This can be before blockers are declared, after blockers are declared but before combat damage is dealt, during combat after combat damage is dealt, during the postcombat main phase, during the end step, or, in some unusual cases, during the cleanup step.","oracle_id":"e0c00a74-bdf8-4fee-8042-42c5878e9e3c","published_at":"2023-11-10","source":"wotc"},
    {"comment":"If a creature with a boast ability is put onto the battlefield attacking, it was never declared as an attacker. Its boast ability can't be activated that turn.","oracle_id":"e0c00a74-bdf8-4fee-8042-42c5878e9e3c","published_at":"2023-11-10","source":"wotc"},
    {"comment":"If an effect adds additional combat phases to a turn and a creature with a boast ability attacks more than once during that turn, its boast ability can still be activated only once.","oracle_id":"e0c00a74-bdf8-4fee-8042-42c5878e9e3c","published_at":"2023-11-10","source":"wotc"},
    {"comment":"If it's not your turn and you gain control of a creature with a boast ability after that creature attacked, you can activate that creature's boast ability if it hasn't been activated yet that turn.","oracle_id":"e0c00a74-bdf8-4fee-8042-42c5878e9e3c","published_at":"2023-11-10","source":"wotc"},
    {"comment":"The back face of a double-faced card doesn't have a mana cost. A double-faced permanent with its back face up has a mana value equal to the mana value of its front face.","oracle_id":"e0c00a74-bdf8-4fee-8042-42c5878e9e3c","published_at":"2023-11-10","source":"wotc"},
    {"comment":"If Rest in Peace is destroyed by a spell, Rest in Peace will be exiled and then the spell will be put into its owner's graveyard.","oracle_id":"087f9ad7-e74f-40e2-8102-1ed2925d0418","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},
    {"comment":"If a card is discarded while Rest in Peace is on the battlefield, abilities that function when a card is discarded (such as madness) still work, even though that card never reaches a graveyard. In addition, spells or abilities that check the characteristics of a discarded card (such as Chandra Ablaze's first ability) can find that card in exile.","oracle_id":"087f9ad7-e74f-40e2-8102-1ed2925d0418","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},
    {"comment":"While Rest in Peace is on the battlefield, abilities that trigger whenever a creature dies won't trigger because cards and tokens are never put into a player's graveyard.","oracle_id":"087f9ad7-e74f-40e2-8102-1ed2925d0418","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},
    {"comment":"A card with devoid is just colorless. It’s not colorless and the colors of mana in its mana cost.","oracle_id":"634d6357-af76-4e25-8c63-81522bc726f5","published_at":"2015-08-25","source":"wotc"},
    {"comment":"Cards with devoid use frames that are variations of the transparent frame traditionally used for Eldrazi. The top part of the card features some color over a background based on the texture of the hedrons that once imprisoned the Eldrazi. This coloration is intended to aid deckbuilding and game play.","oracle_id":"634d6357-af76-4e25-8c63-81522bc726f5","published_at":"2015-08-25","source":"wotc"},
    {"comment":"Devoid works in all zones, not just on the battlefield.","oracle_id":"634d6357-af76-4e25-8c63-81522bc726f5","published_at":"2015-08-25","source":"wotc"},
    {"comment":"Gaining control of a creature doesn’t cause you to gain control of any Auras or Equipment attached to it.","oracle_id":"634d6357-af76-4e25-8c63-81522bc726f5","published_at":"2015-08-25","source":"wotc"},
    {"comment":"If a card loses devoid, it will still be colorless. This is because effects that change an object’s color (like the one created by devoid) are considered before the object loses devoid.","oracle_id":"634d6357-af76-4e25-8c63-81522bc726f5","published_at":"2015-08-25","source":"wotc"},
    {"comment":"Other cards and abilities can give a card with devoid color. If that happens, it’s just the new color, not that color and colorless.","oracle_id":"634d6357-af76-4e25-8c63-81522bc726f5","published_at":"2015-08-25","source":"wotc"},
    {"comment":"Turn Against can target any creature, even one that’s untapped or one you already control.","oracle_id":"634d6357-af76-4e25-8c63-81522bc726f5","published_at":"2015-08-25","source":"wotc"},
